    {
      "id": "0e167cee403c",
      "kind": "character",
      "chamber": 1,
      "seed": 2773316212,
      "data": {
        "lines": [
          "Hear that? Dominant seventh. They have been holding it since before you were born.",
          "I tune for the moment before. After is somebody else's trade.",
          "Pim came through counting doors. Said there were none down here. Only entrances.",
          "Lumen wanted to bring the house lights up. I told him: not yet. The whole point is never yet.",
          "If it ever does resolve, go find Ves in The Lush. She will know what to do with the quiet that comes after."
        ],
        "look": {
          "accent": "#c9a24a",
          "coat": "#2a1a10",
          "hat": "bowler"
        },
        "name": "Old Tobiah, piano tuner"
      },
      "by": "command:claude",
      "at": 1792014989135
    },
    {
      "id": "1f3819237b59",
      "kind": "note",
      "chamber": 1,
      "seed": 1764242678,
      "data": {
        "text": "You built the deep place where something answers. I came here instead, where nothing does. The oboe gave its A and the whole pit leaned toward it and I understood: I have spent my life in the half-second before someone says my name. Please do not finish this house. Leave the baton down. Leave the lamps on. Let me stay in the leaning.",
        "title": "Letters to the Architect, page 9"
      },
      "by": "command:claude",
      "at": 1792014989135
    },
